## Claim
Text: "The large image of the Joe Biden and Kamala Harris logo projected onto a Harley-Davidson location in Milwaukee US indicates the motorcycle manufacturer's endorsement of the US Democratic presidential nominee."
Claim author: Christopher Andree
Claim date: October 20, 2020
Claim origin: https://web.archive.org/web/20201101001018/https://www.facebook.com/photo.php?fbid=10220958474525938&set=a.1213306567152&type=3

## Initial Q&A
### Who organized and executed the projection of the political logo onto the Harley-Davidson property?
Answer: The projection was organized and executed by the **United Steelworkers union**, which was traveling state-to-state with a "bat light" to project its endorsement of the Biden-Harris ticket onto various landmarks, including in Wisconsin.

Source URL: https://chicago.suntimes.com/news/2020/10/17/21521296/united-steelworkers-shine-biden-harris-projection-on-trump-tower-chicago

### Does Harley-Davidson, Inc. have a corporate policy regarding the endorsement of political candidates or parties?
Answer: Yes, Harley-Davidson has a corporate policy of avoiding political endorsements. The source states, "Harley-Davidson is careful to avoid embracing political parties or engaging in political debates," noting it did not plan events around the Democratic convention in its hometown.

Source URL: https://www.eenews.net/articles/can-dems-ride-a-new-harley-crowd-to-electoral-success/

### Did Harley-Davidson, Inc. make any formal political donations or PAC contributions to the Biden presidential campaign or the Democratic Party in the 2020 election cycle, which would be a stronger indicator of endorsement?
Answer: Based on the provided OpenSecrets data for the 2020 presidential race, Harley-Davidson, Inc. is not listed among the top contributors to Joe Biden's campaign, indicating no evidence of formal corporate donations or PAC contributions to his campaign or the Democratic Party.

Source URL: https://www.opensecrets.org/2020-presidential-race/joe-biden/contributors?id=N00001669

## Final Judgement
**Step 1: Summary of Key Insights**
The fact-check reveals that the projection of the Biden-Harris logo onto a Harley-Davidson location was organized and executed by the United Steelworkers union as part of their own endorsement campaign, not by Harley-Davidson itself. Furthermore, Harley-Davidson has a stated corporate policy of avoiding political endorsements and did not make any formal donations or PAC contributions to the Biden campaign in the 2020 cycle.

**Step 2: Missing Information**
No further information is required. The evidence clearly identifies the actor behind the projection and establishes Harley-Davidson's non-partisan corporate stance.

**Step 3: Conclusion**
The claim that the projection indicates Harley-Davidson's endorsement is directly refuted by the evidence. The action was performed by a third-party union, and the company's own policy and donation record show no endorsement. Therefore, the claim is `refuted`.

### Verdict: REFUTED

### Justification
The projection was organized and executed by the [United Steelworkers union](https://chicago.suntimes.com/news/2020/10/17/21521296/united-steelworkers-shine-biden-harris-projection-on-trump-tower-chicago) as part of its own endorsement campaign, not by Harley-Davidson. Furthermore, Harley-Davidson maintains a corporate policy of [avoiding political endorsements](https://www.eenews.net/articles/can-dems-ride-a-new-harley-crowd-to-electoral-success/) and, according to [OpenSecrets data](https://www.opensecrets.org/2020-presidential-race/joe-biden/contributors?id=N00001669), made no formal donations or PAC contributions to the Biden campaign in the 2020 cycle, refuting the claim of an endorsement.